# Don't stop here, keep learning!

## Additional Resources
* #### <a href="https://www.teachai.org/" target="_blank">TeachAI.org</a> Empowering educators to teach with and about AI.
* #### <a href="https://iste-ascd.org/ai" target="_blank">Artificial Intelligence in Education</a> from ISTE.
* #### <a href="https://iacomputinged.org/graiser/" target="_blank">Guidelines for Responsible Use of AI in Education Research</a> from Advancing Computing Education.
* #### <a href="https://aipedagogy.org/" target="_blank">AI Pedagogy Project</a>


## Take it Further Activities

#### Want to learn more? Try out the following optional activities.

  <!-- Dropdown 3 -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">

<summary style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold">
	Check out AI Guidance in your State/Country
</summary>

<div style="margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #ddd;">
<p style="margin: 5px 0 10px 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">The TeachAI AI in Education Guidance and Policy Tracker can help you find AI gudiance for your state or country.
</p>

  <a href="https://www.teachai.org/policy-tracker" 
         target="blank" 
         rel="noopener noreferrer" 
         style="display: inline-block; margin-top: 5px; padding: 8px 12px; background-color: #026C7A; color: #ffffff; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 14px;">Check it Out
</a>
</div>

</details>

  <!-- Dropdown 2 -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">

<summary style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold">
	Create an AI Use Guideline for Your Classroom
</summary>

<div style="margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #ddd;">
<p style="margin: 5px 0 10px 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">Draft a short set of expectations for how students should use AI tools. Include guidelines for privacy, accuracy, and appropriate use. Reference the <a href="https://www.teachai.org/toolkit-guidance" target="_blank">Sample Guidance</a> from TeachAI.org to help you.
</p>
</div>

</details>

  <!-- Dropdown 1 -->
<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">

<summary style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold">
	AI Mini-Lesson
</summary>

<div style="margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid #ddd;">
<p style="margin: 5px 0 10px 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">Design a mini-lesson or activity for your classroom that addresses topics of AI misinformation, bias, or data privacy.
</p>
</div>

</details>

